{"abstract":[{"text":"Walk the abstract syntax tree of a parsed document to extract information or to transform it.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ProcessingMarkdown"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Processing Markdown"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The usage of abstract syntax trees for representing Markdown text has the advantage that it is very easy to process such data, in particular, to transform it and to extract information from it. The syntax tree of a document consists of two recursive data types: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for block-level structure such as headings, paragraphs and lists, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the inline markup inside of blocks, such as emphasis and links. A sequence of text fragments is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Extract-the-outline-of-a-document","level":3,"text":"Extract the outline of a document","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This function extracts the top-level headers of a document. It parses a document and matches on the ","type":"text"},{"code":"document","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"heading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cases of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let markdown = MarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"\"\"","                   # First *Header*","                   ## Sub-header","                   And this is a **paragraph**.","                   # Second **Header**","                   And this is another paragraph.","                 \"\"\")","","func topLevelHeaders(doc: Block) -> [String] {","  guard case .document(let topLevelBlocks) = doc else {","    preconditionFailure(\"markdown block does not represent a document\")","  }","  var outline: [String] = []","  for block in topLevelBlocks {","    if case .heading(1, let text) = block {","      outline.append(text.rawDescription)","    }","  }","  return outline","}","","let headers = topLevelHeaders(doc: markdown)","print(headers)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This will print an array with the following two entries:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["[\"First Header\", \"Second Header\"]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text/rawDescription","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the text of a heading without its markup: the emphasis in ","type":"text"},{"code":"First *Header*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Visit-nested-structure","level":3,"text":"Visit nested structure","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Blocks contain blocks: a block quote contains blocks, a list contains list items, and a list item contains blocks. Text contains text fragments, which can contain text again. A function that looks at the whole document therefore recurses through both types. This example collects the destinations of all links in paragraphs and headings:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func links(inBlock block: Block) -> [String] {","  switch block {","    case .document(let blocks),","         .blockquote(let blocks),","         .list(_, _, let blocks),","         .listItem(_, _, let blocks):","      return blocks.flatMap(links(inBlock:))","    case .paragraph(let text),","         .heading(_, let text):","      return links(inText: text)","    default:","      return []","  }","}","","func links(inText text: Text) -> [String] {","  var result: [String] = []","  for fragment in text {","    switch fragment {","      case .link(let inner, let destination, _):","        result.append(contentsOf: destination.map { [$0] } ?? [])","        result.append(contentsOf: links(inText: inner))","      case .autolink(_, let destination):","        result.append(String(destination))","      case .emph(let inner),","           .strong(let inner),","           .underline(let inner),","           .strikethrough(let inner):","        result.append(contentsOf: links(inText: inner))","      default:","        break","    }","  }","  return result","}","","let doc = MarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"A [link](https://objecthub.com) and <https://swift.org>.\")","print(links(inBlock: doc))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This prints ","type":"text"},{"code":"[\"https://objecthub.com\", \"https://swift.org\"]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The example does not look into tables, definition lists and custom blocks, which only the extended parsers produce (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), or into custom text fragments. A function that has to be complete handles those cases, too: see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UnderstandingTheSyntaxTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the structure of each case.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Process-a-document-in-a-background-task","level":3,"text":"Process a document in a background task","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Syntax trees are values that can be passed between threads. Parse in a background task and use the result wherever you need it. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignment":{"abstract":[{"text":"Column alignments are represented as arrays of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum values","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alignment"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignment","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alignment"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Alignment","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/alignment"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignments":{"abstract":[{"text":"The alignments of the columns of a table: one for each column.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alignments"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignments","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alignments"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Alignments","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/alignments"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AutolinkType":{"abstract":[{"text":"Represents an autolink type.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutolinkType"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AutolinkType","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutolinkType"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AutolinkType","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/autolinktype"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block":{"abstract":[{"text":"Enumeration of Markdown blocks. This enumeration defines the block structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"i.e. the abstract syntax, of Markdown supported by MarkdownKit. The structure of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inline text is defined by the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" struct.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Block","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Blocks":{"abstract":[{"text":"A normalized sequence of blocks, represented as an array.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Blocks"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Blocks","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Blocks"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Blocks","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/blocks"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the parser class that supports the Markdown syntax your documents use.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Choosing a Parser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/choosingaparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definition":{"abstract":[{"text":"A definition of a definition list: a term and its descriptions. A term can have several","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"descriptions (","type":"text"},{"code":": description","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Definition"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definition","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Definition"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Definition","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/definition"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definitions":{"abstract":[{"text":"A sequence of definitions: the content of a definition list.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Definitions"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definitions","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Definitions"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Definitions","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/definitions"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Lines":{"abstract":[{"text":"Lines are arrays of substrings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Lines"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Lines","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Lines"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Lines","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/lines"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListDensity":{"abstract":[{"text":"Describes whether the blocks of a list item are separated by blank lines. The parser uses it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to find out whether the list which contains the item is tight or loose, and records it in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"listItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ListDensity"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListDensity","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ListDensity"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ListDensity","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/listdensity"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListType":{"abstract":[{"text":"Enumeration of Markdown list types.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ListType"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListType","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ListType"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ListType","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/listtype"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Row":{"abstract":[{"text":"Rows are arrays of text.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Row"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Row","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Row"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Row","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/row"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Rows":{"abstract":[{"text":"A sequence of table rows.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rows"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Rows","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rows"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Rows","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/rows"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text":{"abstract":[{"text":"Struct ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used to represent inline text. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct consists of a sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Text","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/text"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text/rawDescription":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a raw description of this ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object as a string, i.e. as if the text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be represented in Markdown but ignoring all markup.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rawDescription"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text/rawDescription","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"rawDescription","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/text/rawdescription"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment":{"abstract":[{"text":"In MarkdownKit, text with markup is represented as a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enumeration variant represents one form of inline markup. Since","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"markup can be arbitrarily nested, this is a recursive data structure (via struct ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextFragment"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextFragment"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TextFragment","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/textfragment"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UnderstandingTheSyntaxTree":{"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how Markdown syntax maps to the cases of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UnderstandingTheSyntaxTree","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Understanding the Syntax Tree","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/understandingthesyntaxtree"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse and generate on background threads and tasks, and know what to restate in subclasses.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Using MarkdownKit Concurrently","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/usingmarkdownkitconcurrently"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Representing-Markdown-documents","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UnderstandingTheSyntaxTree","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Blocks","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListType","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ListDensity","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignment","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Alignments","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Row","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Rows","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definition","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Definitions","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AutolinkType","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Lines"],"title":"Representing Markdown documents"}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/markdownkit/processingmarkdown"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}]}